WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.800
- Good evening, everyone.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.707
And it is a good evening
because we are in it.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.770
(audience applauds)

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.680
I am excited to be present at a gathering

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.890
where this community
acknowledges two people

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.900
in this business to whom I looked early on

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.780
while learning how to walk
in real women's shoes.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.450
I am thrilled to be present
at such an historic moment

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.560
when this academy hails two men

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.000
who are brilliant storytellers,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.780
and also my treasured friends.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.780
I am beside myself that I
get to have the great fortune

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.970
to stand up on a glorious night

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.650
and say to you that I'm bearing witness

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:55.650
to the fact that Danny Glover shows up.

00:00:55.796 --> 00:00:58.640
(audience applauds)

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.980
He always has.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.690
He shows up.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:08.690
He shows up to work, to
play, to build, to assist.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:12.830
His strong hands and a tender reach.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:15.430
He shows up.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:18.390
That is why tonight we honor him

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:22.063
with the Jean Hersholt Humanitarian Award.

00:01:22.063 --> 00:01:25.810
(audience applauds)

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.297
Marian Wright Edelman said,

00:01:27.297 --> 00:01:30.950
"Service is the rent you pay for being."

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.710
It is the very purpose of life

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:36.013
and not something you
do in your spare time.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.360
Danny's purpose-centered
life started early

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.800
at the direction of his parents,

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.870
James and Carrie, both postal workers,

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.360
when they brought their son
along to strategy meetings

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.783
and to the ground-shifting
marches of the Bay Area NAACP.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.950
His mother had grown up
in Jim Crow, Georgia.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.950
His father served with distinction
in the Second World War

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:06.400
where a black man could
die for his country

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.360
and often returned home only to die

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.700
at the hands of his countrymen

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.410
if he dared tried to live the freedoms

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:19.083
he had just risked his
life defending abroad.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.340
In the Glover home,
dignity, respect, freedom,

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.330
and justice were the centerpiece

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.340
at the dinner table discussions.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.590
They were the foundational values

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:36.540
from which Danny grew tall.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:41.323
And he turned into a living
portrait of authentic activism.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.540
It was a time of man when he
set out across the Bay Bridge.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.050
It was the height of the
civil rights movement

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.733
and the fierce resistance to it.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.650
Leaders who advocated that all men

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.640
and women were created equal

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:01.550
under the laws of Heaven and America.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:06.240
Leaders who insisted America
deliver on her promise

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.240
to those upon whose backs
she was built and sustained.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:15.010
Medgar, Malcolm, Martin,

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:18.633
and Bobby were viciously gunned down.

00:03:19.922 --> 00:03:23.263
And Danny Glover stood up even taller.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.470
He hit the books hard,

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:29.113
and he hit the streets with an insistence.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.620
At San Francisco State,
Danny was a driving force

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:36.820
in the longest student
walkout in US history,

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.910
aiming to establish a
Department of Black Studies.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.810
Why?
(audience applauds)

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.750
Because James and Carrie's
generation had fought

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.760
to get universities to
open wide their doors

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.570
to people of color.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:56.570
And Danny recognized that higher education

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:00.930
was incomplete to a farcical degree

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:05.880
when it actively ignored
a crucial defining element

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.253
of American history and culture.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:12.870
His activism helped create the
Department of Black Studies,

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.930
the first one in the United States,

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:18.603
along with the first
School of Ethnic Studies.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.390
I have always gained strength

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.933
from standing shoulder
to shoulder with Danny.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.250
Figuratively.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:29.480
We bonded on film sets

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:33.223
with our shared history
of coming from good folk.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:36.820
He brought me into the understanding

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:41.820
of the struggles of the
liberation of African peoples,

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.570
culminating in our co-founding

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:47.530
of Artists for a Free South
Africa to galvanize support

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.440
for a worldwide anti-apartheid movement,

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.523
and especially to be of
assistance to the leadership.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:57.540
Nelson Mandela welcomed us.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.220
He recognized us as his own

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.160
because our social activity was rooted

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.863
in a love for the people.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.880
He thought Danny a comrade

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.840
because Danny walked
the walk of conscience,

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.453
even if it meant traversing a minefield.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.300
Danny has been willing
to go to jail for justice

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.360
as he did in DC, protesting
at the Sudanese Embassy,

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.510
decrying the staggering atrocities

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:30.743
that created an intolerable
humanitarian crisis in Darfur.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:36.180
For a man who moves with
love and delivers joy,

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.740
Danny is the poster guy
as a UNICEF ambassador,

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.960
and he's been actively
bringing hope, inspiration,

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.240
and healing in that capacity since 2004,

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:52.210
actually, it's since 1995.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:55.550
He builds community
wherever his foot lands.

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:57.520
He levels his light

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:01.453
wherever a fellow traveler
pulls in darkness.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:06.290
Danny Glover always does
the right thing first

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.363
without testing the prevailing
winds of public opinion.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:14.530
The places in his heart
where he has put his time

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:17.673
and his resources outnumber his years.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:19.483
Let's take a look.

